go atlas

#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diagnostic deck for the NEGF mode-space run - revision 4 (minimal)
#
# Rev 3 errored on load with:
#     Error: No mesh lines specified in the X direction.
# right after the standalone `mesh cylindrical` line. Diagnosis: ATLAS
# parses `mesh cylindrical` as the start of a new mesh declaration, not
# as a flag-toggle on the already-loaded mesh, and then demands
# X.MESH/Y.MESH lines that never come.
#
# Fix: drop that line. The non-cylindrical interpretation does not
# matter for pointwise band probes (con.band / val.band at a coordinate
# is the same scalar in either coordinate system).
#
# This revision also strips every other line that could plausibly be
# the failure source, so this deck is the smallest possible probe-and-
# print: load, declare materials, define probes, open log, solve init,
# close log, plot. Anything else that errored in rev 3 is no longer in
# the deck to error.
#
# Things removed vs rev 3:
#   - `mesh cylindrical`        (the actual error in rev 3)
#   - `output con.band ...`     (loaded .str already has output settings)
#   - `master` qualifier on log (bare `log outfile=` is universal)
#   - `models fermi temperature=300`
#   - `method newton`
# (solve init takes whatever statistics the loaded structure had.)
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

mesh infile=gaa_iiiv_hj_tfet_negf_btbt_vd05.str

material material=GaSb   permittivity=15.70 eg300=0.726 affinity=4.06 nc300=2.0e17 nv300=1.3e19
material material=InAs   permittivity=15.15 eg300=0.354 affinity=4.90 nc300=8.7e16 nv300=6.6e18
material material=InGaAs permittivity=13.90 eg300=0.74  affinity=4.50 nc300=2.1e17 nv300=7.7e18
material material=HfO2   permittivity=22.0  eg300=5.7   affinity=2.05

probe name=EC_GaSb       x=0.001 y=0.010 con.band
probe name=EV_GaSb       x=0.001 y=0.010 val.band
probe name=EV_GaSb_junc  x=0.001 y=0.019 val.band
probe name=EC_InAs_junc  x=0.001 y=0.021 con.band
probe name=EC_InAs       x=0.001 y=0.030 con.band
probe name=EV_InAs       x=0.001 y=0.030 val.band
probe name=EC_InGaAs     x=0.001 y=0.050 con.band

# Open a log so probes have somewhere to write.
log outfile=gaa_iiiv_hj_tfet_negf_diag.log

# Fresh equilibrium solve at V = 0 (the loaded .str has no carrier
# solution to continue from). Bands are determined by affinity / Eg
# and equilibrium charge transfer, not the applied bias, so V = 0 is
# sufficient for the alignment check.
solve init

log off

# Plot the log; probe values are also visible by opening the .log
# file in a text editor.
tonyplot gaa_iiiv_hj_tfet_negf_diag.log

#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Interpretation:
#
# Broken-gap is confirmed if EV_GaSb (y=0.010, deep source bulk) is
# greater than EC_InAs (y=0.030, mid-channel bulk). The "+114 meV
# overlap" expected from chi(GaSb)=4.06, chi(InAs)=4.90, Eg(GaSb)=0.726
# is most directly visible in these BULK probes, not the AT-JUNCTION
# probes (the junction probes are pinned together by the equilibrium
# charge-transfer dipole).
#
# ATLAS uses an internal energy reference (typically the source
# contact Fermi level), not vacuum, so the absolute numbers will be
# uniformly shifted from the flat-band expectation. The relative
# difference EV_GaSb - EC_InAs is what matters.
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

quit
